\description{
Adjusts survey weights so that the weighted marginal totals of calibration
variables match known population values using linear (GREG) estimation. Uses
\code{F(u) = 1 + u} which is exact in a single Newton step when \code{bounds = NULL}.
When \code{bounds = c(L, U)} is specified, switches to truncated-linear
calibration where g-weights are constrained to \verb{[L, U]} using
Newton-Raphson iteration.
}
\section{Algorithm}{

Linear calibration uses \eqn{F(u) = 1 + u} (the GREG estimator). The
calibrated weights are
\deqn{w_k = d_k (1 + x_k^T \hat{\lambda})}
where the Lagrange multipliers satisfy
\deqn{\hat{\lambda} = \left(\sum_{k \in s} d_k x_k x_k^T\right)^{-1}
  \left(X_U - \sum_{k \in s} d_k x_k\right).}
The solution is obtained in a single Newton step (no iteration required)
when \code{bounds = NULL}.

When \code{bounds = c(L, U)} is specified, g-weights are constrained to
\verb{[L, U]} (truncated-linear calibration) via Newton-Raphson iteration.
}

\section{Convergence}{

For unbounded calibration (\code{bounds = NULL}), the solution is exact in
one step — no convergence check is performed.

For bounded calibration, Newton-Raphson terminates when the maximum
absolute change in \eqn{\lambda} falls below \code{control$epsilon} (default
\code{1e-7}), or when \code{control$maxit} (default \code{50}) iterations are reached.
Calibration non-convergence raises an error.
}

